FILE:      T2R_variance_decomposition.csv
SHA256:    00e4ece086f1d513c3f622228ea453d13cb83c8a91b4b19c696468c9131cfe2b
PRODUCER:  code/S10R_exhibits.R (SHA256: 8cbc22f6817800b7062b08dc52439240843807e648fca7c675083993c8ef14be)
DESCRIPTION: Variance decomposition with bootstrap SEs (FIXED CHAIN)
CREATED:   2026-07-26 06:50:28
WARNING: Column names in this file are misleading. Corrected mapping (SYNC-6e):
  - "Var_theta_hat" = 2.49610882 is Var(theta_B), NOT Var(theta_D).
      sqrt(2.49610882) = 1.57991 = T5R SD_theta_B.
  - "SD_theta_D" = 1.56139375 is SD(theta_D); its square, 2.43795, is the
      ledgered VAR_THETA_D (2.4380), which passes gate G1 in T21_arms.
  - "Var_theta" = 2.32436 = Var_theta_hat - Mean_SE_sq, a decomposition of
      Var(theta_B), not of Var(theta_D).
  - "Mean_SE_sq" = 0.171745 is mean(se_B^2) ONLY. The noise-only arm subtracts
      mean(se_total^2) = 0.261145, where se_total^2 = se_B^2 + sd_cf^2
      (INV-022; T11 gives 0.171745 + 0.089447 = 0.261193).
  - "SD_theta_true" = 1.52459 follows from the two lines above and is therefore
      NOT any arm reported in T21_arms.
  For Var(theta_D) cite T21_arms.csv (VAR_THETA_D, gate G1); for arm-indexed
  SD_true cite T21_arms.csv. Do not cite Var_theta_hat as Var(theta_D).
  Supersedes the SYNC-5 warning, which asserted the inverse and would have put
  the wrong denominator under every arm share.
